 

@startuml part2_status_lifecycle_and_cancellation
actor Resident
actor Staff
actor Admin
participant API
database DB

== 1. Status update (In Progress / Resolved) ==
Staff -> API: PATCH /complaints/{id}/status
alt staff not assigned to complaint
  API --> Staff: 403 Staff not assigned to this complaint
else invalid status transition
  API --> Staff: 422 Invalid status transition
else valid
  API -> DB: Update complaint status
  API -> DB: Record progress log entry for new status
  API -> DB: Notify resident and admin
  API --> Staff: 200 OK
end

== 2. Resolution comment (staff) ==
Staff -> API: POST /complaints/{id}/comments (Resolution)
alt complaint not Resolved
  API --> Staff: 422 Complaint not Resolved
else valid
  API -> DB: Save resolution comment
  API --> Staff: 201 Created
end

== 3. Feedback comment (resident) → auto-close ==
Resident -> API: POST /complaints/{id}/comments (Feedback, staffRating)
alt rating missing or out of range 1-5
  API --> Resident: 422 Rating missing/out of range
else feedback already submitted
  API --> Resident: 422 Feedback already submitted
else valid
  API -> DB: Save feedback comment with staff rating
  API -> DB: Update complaint status to Closed
  API -> DB: Record progress log entry for Closed status
  API -> DB: Notify admin and staff
  API --> Resident: 201 Created (complaintStatus=Closed)
end

== 4. Resident cancellation ==
Resident -> API: PATCH /complaints/{id}/cancel (cancellationReason)
alt complaint not Assigned or already cancelled
  API --> Resident: 422 Complaint not in Assigned status / already cancelled
else valid
  API -> DB: Mark complaint as Cancelled with reason and timestamp
  API -> DB: Release availability slot and unlink from complaint
  API -> DB: Record progress log entry for Cancelled status
  API -> DB: Notify staff and admin
  API --> Resident: 200 OK (slotFreed=true)
end

== 5. Admin reassign after escalation ==
Admin -> API: PATCH /complaints/{id}/assignments/{aid}/reassign
alt new slot already booked / assignment not reassignable
  API --> Admin: 422 New slot booked / not reassignable
else new staff or slot not found
  API --> Admin: 404 New staff or slot not found
else valid
  API -> DB: Mark existing assignment as Reassigned
  API -> DB: Create new assignment for replacement staff with Pending Acceptance status
  API -> DB: Notify new staff, resident, and admin
  API --> Admin: 200 OK
end

== 6. Admin resolves escalation ==
Admin -> API: PATCH /complaints/{id}/escalation (status=Resolved)
alt escalation already resolved or complaint not Closed
  API --> Admin: 422 Already resolved / complaint not Closed
else no escalation record found
  API --> Admin: 404 No escalation record found
else valid
  API -> DB: Mark escalation as resolved with resolution date
  API --> Admin: 200 OK
end
@enduml
